## 14. SVELTE 5 REACTIVITY PATTERNS

**Deep State Mutation:**
```typescript
// Svelte 5 $state with deep reactivity
const messages = $state<AggregatedMessage[]>([]);

// Direct mutations trigger reactivity
messages.push(newMessage);          // Works!
messages[0].content += "more";      // Works!
```

**Derived Values:**
```typescript
const showJumpButton = $derived(() => !shouldAutoScroll && isStreaming());
const isThinking = $derived(() => messages.length > 0 && lastMessage.type === 'user_message');
```

**Effects:**
```typescript
$effect(() => {
  // Access dependencies to create reactive graph
  displayLines;  // dependency
  
  // Implementation runs when dependency changes
  if (autoScroll) scrollToBottom();
});
```

**Careful Array Handling:**
```typescript
// GOOD: Always lookup from reactive array
const msg = messages.find((m) => m.id === id);
if (msg && 'content' in msg) {
  msg.content += "more";  // Proxy mutation works
}

// BAD: Direct reference loses reactivity
const msg = messageById.get(id);
msg.content += "more";  // Mutation bypasses $state proxy!
```

